### What would you like to be added?

 Purpose:
 Checks if a GitHub Actions artifact exists in the current workflow run.
 Used to conditionally download artifacts and avoid errors when artifacts
 are missing or haven't been created yet.


 Key Features:
 - Validates artifact is not expired and has non-zero size
 - Returns false if artifact name is empty (disables artifact checking)
 - Handles API errors gracefully without failing the workflow



  ```
 # Query GitHub REST API to check if an artifact with the given name exists
    # This only works for artifacts uploaded with actions/upload-artifact@v4
    - name: artifact exists
      uses: actions/github-script@v8
      id: artifact-exists
      with:
        script: |
          const artifactName = "${{inputs.artifact_name}}";

          // If artifact name is empty, skip the check (allows disabling artifact lookup)
          if (!artifactName) {
              console.log("Artifact name is empty. Not looking for any github artifact.");
              core.setOutput("exists", false);
              return;
          }

          try {
              // Call GitHub REST API to list all artifacts from this workflow run
              const response = await github.rest.actions.listWorkflowRunArtifacts({
                owner: context.repo.owner,
                repo: context.repo.repo,
                run_id: context.runId
              });
              console.log(response.data)

              const artifacts = response.data.artifacts;

              // Search for artifact matching the name, and verify it's valid:
              // - Not expired (still accessible)
              // - Has content (size > 0 bytes)
              const artifactExists =  artifacts.find(a =>
                  a.name === artifactName &&
                  !a.expired &&
                  a.size_in_bytes > 0
              );

              // Output boolean indicating whether a valid artifact was found
              core.setOutput("exists", Boolean(artifactExists));
          } catch (e) {
            // Handle errors gracefully - don't fail the workflow
            console.error("Error listing artifacts", e);
            core.setOutput("exists", false);
          }
```

### Why is this needed?

To prevent failure if the artifact is missing, allow customize the behaviur easily if the artifact is mising
